            description: "Medium, globose, yellow, yellow-fleshed clingstone ripening in early to mid-July. The flesh is soft and very juicy, with excellent flavor. The tree is vigorous, spreading, large, and moderately productive with low susceptibility to bacterial spot. It is pollinated by Methley, Vanier and other Asian type varieties"
